  "title": "Unusual Sessions",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "f5e7a266-39cd-4430-8790-8c7f59fa3c0b",
      "question": "Treat January 2 through June 30, 2026 as the baseline for every issuer. Which 10 issuer sessions from July 1 through August 31, 2026 were the most unusual in return, volatility and volume, and which features made each one unusual? Anomaly scores are neither forecasts nor explanations.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T04:27:13.757479Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T04:27:40.246033Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Top‑10 most unusual issuer‑sessions (July 1 – August 31 2026)**\n*Baseline = Jan 2 – Jun 30 2026; “unusual” = highest anomaly score from the market‑anomaly scan (all assets).  Scores are robust‑z‑score based; they are descriptive, not forecasts.*\n\n| Rank | Asset (ticker) | Session (UTC) | Anomaly score | Features driving the anomaly (robust z‑scores) |\n|------|----------------|---------------|---------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| 1 | **DREI** | 2026‑07‑08 | 16.56 | • Adj‑return 1d = **‑25.96**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **‑11.56**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+14.41**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **+14.81** |\n| 2 | **MOST** | 2026‑07‑27 | 15.04 | • Adj‑return 1d = **‑2.53**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **+10.24**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+12.42**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **+0.88** |\n| 3 | **DREI** | 2026‑07‑09 | 14.98 | • Adj‑return 1d = **+0.95**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **‑11.44**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+14.41**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **+0.37** |\n| 4 | **FLOA** | 2026‑07‑02 | 13.64 | • Adj‑return 1d = **‑2.42**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **+9.91**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+12.49**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **‑0.58** |\n| 5 | **DREI** | 2026‑07‑14 | 12.93 | • Adj‑return 1d = **+0.61**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **‑10.89**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+14.36**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **+0.60** |\n| 6 | **DREI** | 2026‑07‑10 | 11.62 | • Adj‑return 1d = **‑1.13**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **‑11.80**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+14.33**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **+0.27** |\n| 7 | **MOST** | 2026‑07‑21 | 11.56 | • Adj‑return 1d = **+23.62**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **+8.72**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+12.19**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **+13.86** |\n| 8 | **FLOA** | 2026‑07‑01 | 10.86 | • Adj‑return 1d = **+0.49**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **+11.29**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+12.31**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **‑1.13** |\n| 9 | **REXI** | 2026‑07‑06 | 10.64 | • Adj‑return 1d = **‑1.71**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **+9.17**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+12.78**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **‑0.61** |\n|10| **DREI** | 2026‑07‑13 | 10.57 | • Adj‑return 1d = **‑2.10**  <br>• Adj‑return 5d = **‑12.25**  <br>• Realized vol 20d = **+14.32**  <br>• Log‑volume dev 20d = **+1.05** |\n\n**What the feature deviations mean**\n\n| Feature | Interpretation of a large positive/negative z‑score |\n|---------|----------------------------------------------------|\n| **adjusted_return_1d** | One‑day price move far from the baseline distribution (positive = unusually large gain, negative = unusually large loss). |\n| **adjusted_return_5d** | Five‑day cumulative return far from baseline (same sign convention). |\n| **realized_volatility_20d** | 20‑day realized volatility far above (positive) or below (negative) its historic range. |\n| **log_volume_deviation_20d** | Log‑volume over the past 20 sessions far above (positive) or below (negative) typical levels. |\n\n**Key take‑aways**\n\n* The **DREI** ticker dominates the list (5 of the top‑10), mainly because its 20‑day volatility and volume deviate strongly (+14 z) while its multi‑day returns are deeply negative.\n* **MOST** shows two extreme sessions: a large positive 1‑day return (+23.6 z) with high volume (+13.9 z) on 2026‑07‑21, and a mixed‑sign pattern on 2026‑07‑27.\n* **FLOA** and **REXI** each appear once, driven by a combination of elevated 5‑day returns and higher‑than‑usual volatility.\n\n**Limitations** – The anomaly scores describe unusual *observed* feature combinations; they are **not forecasts, probabilities, or causal explanations**[1].\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market anomaly scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:6a2b1509c734f6bbc33c3742dfb3dec86009136d7b3366eb32aa13082c27916d`",
